{"title":"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 28","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_angle\" title=\"Right angle\">right angle</a> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/1/3512e41cc833f3f47fe00df2b822406fdee2f163.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB &gt; CA$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" />. Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is located on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> so that angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/e/81e7cd9b45373c3557d9c584c85b2919b46adfed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CAD$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> is twice angle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e94f1abd32d37d04a5b77e333689bf70ef83864.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DAB$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d7d739c0152a4c6e31d6ec2aa9eb9f15b33336.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC/AD = 2/3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/354af963062b8714f04734c64ad574560520e7e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD/BD = m/n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/9/c49a9ccfe7d87a1c5ad1d08830d83f8cf39dd4cd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A) \\ }10 \\qquad \\mathrm{(B) \\ }14 \\qquad \\mathrm{(C) \\ }18 \\qquad \\mathrm{(D) \\ }22 \\qquad \\mathrm{(E) \\ } 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"387\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/6/aa67d5eedcc6ce1a128570abbdde6cbbfb208442.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta = \\angle DAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"92\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/27828c6a1c625a87fb4dda1413ea9ba9c33c942c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\theta = \\angle CAD$\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/6/dd672fa2c1b53e9e45df05506c540aa769f18fda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\theta = \\angle CAB$\" width=\"97\" height=\"13\" />. Then, it is given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e4bbe3c53fa3353d20ca1d56e11f319de5e1c4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 2\\theta = \\frac{AC}{AD} = \\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"138\" height=\"38\" /> and\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/9/7f9e8b19b091fcc2af041035e6e91d142adff013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BD}{CD} = \\frac{AC(\\tan 3\\theta - \\tan 2\\theta)}{AC \\tan 2\\theta} = \\frac{\\tan 3\\theta}{\\tan 2\\theta} - 1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"332\" height=\"38\" /></center>\n<p><br />\nNow, through the use of trigonometric identities, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/a/d0a96df4e7a98defb8d3912086e30ea1b1cb0b44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos 2\\theta = 2\\cos^2 \\theta - 1 = \\frac{2}{\\sec ^2 \\theta} - 1 = \\frac{1 - \\tan^2 \\theta}{1 + \\tan ^2 \\theta} = \\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"400\" height=\"41\" />. Solving yields that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/6/0d68ef4cfdfa4cc34d94e4ae04a1a4e350a4cdeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan^2 \\theta = \\frac 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"81\" height=\"37\" />. Using the tangent addition identity, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/d/54d75d556949628c7547b95027d6a5fecd3fe8c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan 2\\theta = \\frac{2\\tan \\theta}{1 - \\tan ^2 \\theta},\\ \\tan 3\\theta = \\frac{3\\tan \\theta - \\tan^3 \\theta}{1 - 3\\tan^2 \\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"358\" height=\"40\" />, and\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/5/785e8db7854afad3f4a10fe4e5419fc5764eb10a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BD}{CD} = \\frac{\\tan 3\\theta}{\\tan 2\\theta} - 1 = \\frac{(3 - \\tan^2 \\theta)(1-\\tan ^2 \\theta)}{2(1 - 3\\tan^2 \\theta)} - 1 = \\frac{(1 + \\tan^2 \\theta)^2}{2(1 - 3\\tan^2 \\theta)} = \\frac{9}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"559\" height=\"44\" /></center>\n<p><br />\nand <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d5912eae28d7d8f50ccbd07a279dda91e1c92d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CD}{BD} = \\frac{5}{9} \\Longrightarrow m+n = 14 \\Longrightarrow \\mathbf{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"269\" height=\"37\" />. (This also may have been done on a calculator by finding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> directly)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the application of ratio lemma for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/3/923e3c76f218a042629491e66a5e416659dbb3ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CD}{BD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"32\" height=\"37\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/6/196370697b3fb258fcb6b2a29457455b4d980596.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CD}{BD} = 2\\cos{3A}\\cos{A}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"164\" height=\"37\" />, where we let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/1/cb1e72e1c1679bd78cc3c17fdc6f2328fb3d6adb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A = \\angle{DAB}$\" width=\"94\" height=\"13\" />. We already know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/7/1d78f10c4c590169f9be0e0e83e5f1f2477f004f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{2A}$\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" /> hence the rest is easy\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/d/53d084de05e313a40923ec33ee357544b1b93874.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC=2$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e867467073fae9550c977a21ee2cb19426c4f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD=3$\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />. By the Pythagorean Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851bb3c51e79ecbffe223263df26f90a460906aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=\\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />. Let point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> bisects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/1/4f105551f628f107282e0cc6c89063f3c1faece9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAD$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, angles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/4/6b46d13cd99c1748fbada9584a2fc2a55168d855.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CAP$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/a/70aa9d3cbb9cdbdf811d6d88e5e27ad24fcc8bd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PAD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e94f1abd32d37d04a5b77e333689bf70ef83864.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DAB$\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> are congruent. Applying the angle bisector theorem on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6ce2cd123db24a7b8373999aea7a98927e3b3c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/8/9a8c73e4fea67b41f2615e839a32823118cd455d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CP=\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"88\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/3/a53b4b903fc9c28cec36393ab2fab48a19e959de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PD=\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"93\" height=\"43\" />. Pythagorean Theorem gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/0/390dadda890cc5449c81413e42f0a81f9c97b500.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}\\sqrt{24}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"112\" height=\"41\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/f/d1fdd0172fe04f310e0e4dd9cc523093bbb260f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DB=x$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" />. By the Pythagorean Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/0816b4ddcdeb967a50b6f2c6a713dddab70221a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=\\sqrt{(x+\\sqrt{5})^{2}+2^2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"188\" height=\"32\" />. Applying the angle bisector theorem again on triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92b38136cabb69ee2f7b5711190e0042354f3419.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$APB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fdd1579ce9e7cab87cbce84959abdf858f629be4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\sqrt{(x+\\sqrt{5})^{2}+2^2}}{x}=\\frac{\\frac{\\sqrt{5}\\sqrt{24}}{5}}{\\frac{3\\sqrt{5}}{5}}\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"61\" />\nThe right side simplifies to<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb295b14127eb14994b55757a12a7e3a2d2f87bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sqrt{24}}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"35\" height=\"41\" />. Cross multiplying, squaring, and simplifying, we get a quadratic: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/3/7e38279df804cea4a25158b5a5231c7c3c99f2df.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5x^2-6\\sqrt{5}x-27=0\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"18\" /> Solving this quadratic and taking the positive root gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/5/db5ea5df27e0f505e2cb0b315302dfb4f3c34d4c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x=\\frac{9\\sqrt{5}}{5}\\]\" width=\"70\" height=\"41\" /> Finally, taking the desired ratio and canceling the roots gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/2/89277464e16a29db9d593a2a109da06c975242aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CD}{BD}=\\frac{5}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"70\" height=\"37\" />. The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/f/e9f24a03d32a7a076d4fdb1888fc6713d18ea13a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\fbox{(B) 14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"58\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/6/286e989082359d570543d0269004ce484008ce68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 2$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/4/f142d92351c7c9e5a27f8a5c133742642df1c495.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"64\" height=\"14\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7545963ab5a11c3d2bdfcfdc0af23857e8f8edd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos \\angle CAD = \\frac23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"123\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>By the pythagorean theorem <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/1/3a14433e57b186fefb7e0cfeb86fbdda9db3d597.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = \\sqrt{3^2-2^2} = \\sqrt{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"175\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/f/e0f7f7dafb47c5c49993a6a99a950315379e4380.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\angle BDA = \\sin (180^{\\circ} - \\angle BDA) = \\sin \\angle CDA = \\cos \\angle (90^{\\circ} - CDA) = \\cos \\angle CAD = \\frac23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"680\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25d8172ba30be4f7ec3250bbef7d5075a5d07ff1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin \\angle BAD = \\sqrt{ \\frac{1-cos (2\\angle BAD)}{2} } = \\sqrt{ \\frac{1-\\cos \\angle CAD}{2} } = \\sqrt{ \\frac{1-\\frac23}{2} } = \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"568\" height=\"56\" />\n</p><p>By the Law of Sine, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/e/81e0312d43de5efdabd48d750e646b4dcd8bd9fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{ \\sin \\angle BDA }{AB} = \\frac{ \\sin \\angle BAD }{BD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"198\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/3/0632d155459403436280b1f83b0c254eea65f5c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{ \\frac23 }{ \\sqrt{2^2 + ( \\sqrt{5} + BD)^2} } = \\frac{ \\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6} }{BD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -31px\" width=\"219\" height=\"64\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/6/e1697ddfeb7d4ba9ac98dcd9c9b9ce97a15e9ced.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8BD^2 = 3(9+ 2BD \\sqrt{5} + BD^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"251\" height=\"24\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/1750362244cca443597fb650b4546f89ba7c7c60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5BD^2 - 6 BD \\sqrt{5} -27=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"208\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>As <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/1/ae1f0b3094bbf39c52cf93ed2f2963abf86fb991.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/4/214fe19993aeab1aff44f0db4309434b9a09be87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = \\frac{6 \\sqrt{5} + \\sqrt{ (6 \\sqrt{5})^2 - 4 \\cdot 5 (-27) } }{10} = \\frac{9\\sqrt{5}}{5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"350\" height=\"54\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/c/c0c95b7d584606b0249dc71c36fc03782ba4b2d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CD}{BD} = \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{\\frac{9\\sqrt{5}}{5}} = \\frac59$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"130\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/d/61da02cc998a5b072e2e96747df7b6b06c3acbc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5+9=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) } 14}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"131\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Isabelchen\">isabelchen</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_28&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME\" title=\"1998 AHSME\">1998 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1998 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1998\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_27\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 27\">Problem 27</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1998_AHSME_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"1998 AHSME Problems/Problem 29\">Problem 29</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=199